{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"RESOLVED (RED->GREEN, replicated).\n\nFix: added rebar.llm.model_classes.primary_endpoint_for(resolved) (mirrors fallback_targets_for) and, at the single chokepoint runner.run, when cfg.base_url is unset, recover the matching class slot's endpoint from the resolved model string and apply it as cfg.base_url. This registers rebar's OpenAI-compatible builder for the PRIMARY model, stamps the endpoint host into signed provenance, and flips tier=best_effort — uniformly with the top-level REBAR_LLM_BASE_URL path. No-op when no slot endpoint matches or base_url is already set; the model_override (offline TestModel) path is exempt.\n\nRED->GREEN: tests/unit/test_openai_compatible_provider.py::test_per_class_endpoint_routes_the_primary_through_the_local_builder failed with 'Missing credentials' (stock OpenAIProvider, model=openai:local-model) before the fix; passes after. Full guard: 113 provider/runner/model-class tests + 98 runner-hardening/qualifier + 140 enrich/screen/overlap tests all green; make lint + make typecheck clean; both edited modules under the 800 LOC cap.\n\nReplicated original report: enrich(text=...) with REBAR_LLM_TRIVIAL_ENDPOINT set and NO REBAR_LLM_BASE_URL now returns a schema-valid ticket_digest end-to-end against the real local MLX server (~39s), where it previously raised LLMUnavailableError: Missing credentials.\n\nDocs: docs/llm-framework.md updated — the per-class endpoint recipe is restored as working alongside the top-level base_url recipe, plus a validated local-model worked example."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785883013904148001,"uuid":"c382b5f3-e22f-4457-8080-79efbd61b120"}